{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Signed plan-review PASS at merged SHA 019e32e03d after remediation. Critical reset-hard concern is resolved: no recovery ref pins the old ~1 GiB graph; auto-adoption is limited to pre-epoch -> valid-epoch when the pre-fetch local tip is an ancestor of the readable prior remote, proving no local-only commit. All ahead/diverged/ambiguous states preserve the exact local tip. Execution note for the remaining G6 advisory: the ensure script first snapshots/fetches only to gate reclaim adoption; compatible cases delegate entirely to reconverge, whose own second explicit-refspec fetch and under-lock reclassification are authoritative. A remote advance between those fetches is benign because reconverge consumes the newer tip, and this runs before the review-bot app accepts work. P6 compound lines are parameterized state matrices or one operator receipt; their individual assertions remain separate in the oracle."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785831277696771001,"uuid":"108f5cea-aa29-4bfd-b329-ed2b2746d9b6"}